{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/996697-octavo-s-low-hassle-m20-to-cofd-conversion","id":996697,"title":"Octavo's low hassle M20 to CofD conversion","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-01T11:12:19-07:00","id":996697,"title":"Octavo's low hassle M20 to CofD conversion","content":"<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cinzel\">Mage: the Ascension 20 Translated to Chronicles of Darkness</span></span></span></div> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cinzel\">Design goals</span></span></b></span><ul><li>Ascension setting compatible with the Chronicles of Darkness core book.</li> <li>Ascension magic with a dice mechanics system that has an intuitive probability curve.</li> <li>A simpler downtime magic item creation system.</li> <li>A minimum of cross checking between editions. Ideally, once a few combat and conversion charts and casting charts are printed, the only necessary book should be M20.</li> </ul><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cinzel\">Spell Casting</span></span></b></span><ul><li>Use M20 descriptions to determine what Spheres can do at each rating.</li> <li>Certain Skills and Specialties may be required for the Effect based on the Mage\u2019s Focus/Paradigm. A new Void Engineer recruit can\u2019t build a starship no matter what level her spheres are at if she doesn\u2019t have engineering skills.</li> <li>Dice Pool = Arete + Highest Sphere used in Effect.</li> <li>Use the Magical Reference Charts on page M20 502 with the following modifications.<ul><li>The Spell fully succeeds on 1 success.</li> <li>On the <i>Correspondence Sphere Ranges</i>, <i>Base Damage or Duration, Optional Dividing Successes Rule, Teleportation Locations, Feats of Illusion, and Time Sphere Timelines</i>, the first level of the chart requires no penalty. Moving further down the chart adds a cumulative -2 penalty to the casting roll.</li> <li>Any time a penalty is paid to move up any of the above charts, the caster may move up the <i>Magickal Feats </i>chart at no additional cost.</li> <li>To attempt anything on the <i>Feats of Time Magick</i> chart, the top level of the chart starts at a -4 penalty. Rewinding time adds an additional -3 penalty. Yeesh, this seems unnecessarily harsh.</li> </ul></li> <li>Use the <i>Magickal Difficulty Modifiers </i>chart on M20 page 503 to add bonuses to the casting dice pool. Remember that -1 difficulty in cWoD means +1 bonus in CofD.</li> <li>Willpower adds a +3 bonus to the casting dicepool, but does not guarantee an auto-success.</li> <li>If the dice pool has been reduced to zero, the Mage may try casting with a chance die. This can only be done once per scene or game session. ST discretion. Alternatively, dice pools that exceed a -5 penalty cannot even be attempted with a chance die.</li> <li>Given that the above penalties mount up so high, there\u2019s no reason to increase difficulty based on vulgarity. Vulgarity still adds additional paradox points.</li> </ul><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cinzel\">Additional Effect considerations</span></span></b></span><ul><li>Soak does not exist in CofD. Consider modifying an Effect to add Health Levels, Defense, or Armor instead.</li> <li>Spells that are aimed with a wand or gun can inflict additional levels of damage per success scored from the the Attribute + Firearms or Occult attack pool. However, they can also be dodged entirely.</li> <li>Multiple actions per turn do not exist in CofD. Look at the Celerity Discipline or similar speed spells in the Awakening 2E core for inspiration.</li> </ul><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cinzel\">Paradox</span></span></b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Use the paradox rules on page 549. Due to the levels of damage at upper levels exceeding player maximum health totals, I recommend only using the non-damage effects. Perhaps retain paradox burn damage for Wonders and Umbral Ships. Alternatively, use the Paradox system from the Mage Translation Guide. Paradox will accumulate faster, but do less damage. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cinzel\">Wonder Creation</span></span></b></span><ul><li>Start with the mundane building equipment system on CofD core page 100.</li> <li>Certain skill specialties, such as Energy Weapons, may be required to make Hypertech.</li> <li>Requires Prime 4.</li> <li>Cost: 5 points of Quintessence per Background dot/Arete rating of the Wonder plus 1 point per Sphere used in the Wonder\u2019s effect.</li> </ul><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cinzel\">Character Creation</span></span></b></span><ul><li>Use the CofD mortal template with 10 dots of Merits.</li> <li>Instead of Virtues, use Nature and Demeanor.</li> <li>Add 1 dot of Arete.</li> <li>Optionally, select Tradition, Craft, or Convention.</li> <li>Create Focus and select enough instruments to create a variety of Sphere effects.</li> <li>Select an Affinity Sphere. This sphere must have the highest rating when character creation is complete.</li> <li>Add 6 dots of Spheres, capped at 3 dots.</li> <li>WoD Merits and Backgrounds can be purchased dot for dot via CofD Merit dots.</li> <li>WoD Flaws add CofD Merit dots capped at 7.</li> <li>The Integrity/Wisdom analoge is Quiet, which starts at 0.</li> </ul><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Cinzel\">Character Advancement</span></span></b></span><ul><li>Gain beats and Experiences through the methods listed in the CofD core book.</li> <li>Alternatively, use the M20 method of Experience granting. Consider converting those experience points into beats.</li> <li>Use the CofD Experience chart to determine experience costs.</li> <li>Once a Sphere has reached 3 dots, it is capped by Arete.</li> <li>Affinity Spheres cost 4 Experiences.</li> <li>Non-Affinity Spheres cost 5 Experiences.</li> <li>Arete costs 5 Experiences.</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-01T21:51:11-07:00","id":997005,"title":"","content":"A couple questions: can Arete be raised during character creation as per normal, and does Arete dots hard cap Sphere dots as per normal when less than 3 dots? It looks like no on both counts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6384-frozenfishy","name":"Frozenfishy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T00:41:08-07:00","id":997039,"title":"","content":"If only there was a book of some kind to aid in this kind of work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Writer, Game Designer, Pro since 99.<br /> <br /> Thoughts at <a href=\"http://mobunited.com\" target=\"_blank\">mobunited.com</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/164-malcolm","name":"Malcolm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-02T06:36:26-07:00","id":997108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frozenfishy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/996697-octavo-s-low-hassle-m20-to-cofd-conversion?p=997005#post997005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A couple questions: can Arete be raised during character creation as per normal, and does Arete dots hard cap Sphere dots as per normal when less than 3 dots? It looks like no on both counts.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd probably say Arete dots can be purchased for 5 merit dots, much like Gnosis. I didn't want Arete to cap Spheres until 3 since CofD characters get fewer merit dots and no freebie points. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malcolm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/996697-octavo-s-low-hassle-m20-to-cofd-conversion?p=997039#post997039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If only there was a book of some kind to aid in this kind of work.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really like the Mage Translation Guide! I just wanted something I could use that referenced page numbers of M20 instead of Revised, and used a single success casting system more like Awakening 2E rather than multiple success economy of 1E.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}